      },
      "question": {
        ":question/id": "b3408555-de68-5409-ab55-f212404a9d43",
        ":question/problem": "Consider a rectangle such that the height is fixed but its base $b$ can vary. What is the best interpretation of ${A}^{\u2032}(b)$ if $A$ is the area of the rectangle?",
        ":question/worked-solution": "The function $A(b)$ gives the area of a rectangle with base $b.$ So\n\n$$\n{A}^{\u2032}(b)=\\frac{\\text{d}A}{\\text{d}b}=\\frac{\\text{Change in\u00a0}A}{\\text{Change in\u00a0}b}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${A}^{\u2032}(b)$ is the rate at which the area changes as the base changes.",
        ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
